<title>GERMANY: Messer Griesheim eyes Bombay Oxygen.</title>
<headline>Messer Griesheim eyes Bombay Oxygen.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>German industrial gas producer Messer Griesheim GmbH said on Friday it planned to acquire a majority in Indian industrial gas producer Bombay Oxygen.</p>
<p>Messer Griesheim said it wanted to acquire 50 percent plus one share in the Indian company, which posted sales of about 10 million marks last year. The group supplies the chemical and steel industry with oxygen, argon and nitrogen.</p>
<p>The Messer group, a unit of German chemicals giant Hoechst AG, holds stakes in some 100 different companies and posted 2.5 billion marks in turnover last year.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
